      "message": "feat(machine): Tormach 770M+ and 1100M+ - the M with the MX's axis speeds\n\nThe M+ is an upgrade kit with no manual of its own; per Tormach (via the\ncontributor, 2026-11-09) everything is the M's except the axis speeds,\nwhich are the MX's. Both ship as built-in Tormach mills for the PathPilot\npost: 770M+ = 770M travels/spindle/belts/1.1 kW, 300/300/250 IPM; 1100M+\n= 1100M travels/70-7500 rpm/1.5 kW, 300/300/230 IPM; neither rigid-taps.\n\nPinned by tormach_machines::an_m_plus_is_its_m_with_the_mx_axis_speeds\n(compares the shipped files), every_tormach_machine_states_its_manuals_\nfigures (+2 rows), a_rigid_tap_is_refused_on_a_machine_that_cannot_\nrigid_tap (+2) and machine::every_shipped_machine_mounts_and_speaks_its_\ndeclaration.\n\nFixes #618\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
